feat(sprint-7): identity-preview showcase + apply marks/dots to /ventures

Showcase route /admin/identity-preview (admin-only via
requireAdminContext from team-inbound substrate). Renders all six
ventures plus a synthetic generic-fallback row, with all five
identity components, in BOTH light and dark mode side-by-side.
Edge-case panel for Sparkline at the top of each panel shows
empty / single point / flat / all-zero / negative.

Per-venture grid pulls live ventures rows. Each row renders the
mark at three sizes (16, 22, 34) so the legibility-at-16px
requirement is visually verifiable. StateDot rendered in all three
states. Two ConnectionChip examples per row.

The dark-mode panel is wrapped in a `dark` class to flip globals.css
custom properties — the only place in the app where a single page
intentionally renders in both themes simultaneously.

/ventures listing refactored to consume the new components:
- VentureMark (size 22) prepended to each row, accent flowing in
  via accent_color
- StateDot mapped from venture.phase (build/launch=active,
  scale=idle, discovery/dormant=quiet)
- PhaseBadge retained as the existing semantic badge

/portfolio NOT modified — current page lists portfolio-audit
Documents, not ventures. There's no inline mark/dot to refactor.
Sprint 8 (Bridge) will rebuild /portfolio as the venture canvas;
that's where the venture-identity surface for portfolio lives.

Tests:
- tests/components/venture/sparkline.test.tsx (8 tests). Covers
  empty / single point / flat / all-zero / negative / standard
  ascending / accent style / custom dimensions. Uses
  renderToStaticMarkup, no DOM library required.
- vitest.config.ts include extended to .test.tsx so JSX tests run.

Quality:
- pnpm typecheck clean
- pnpm lint clean
- 58 tests pass (8 new for sparkline)
- pnpm build clean — /admin/identity-preview registered

